{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback","id":228874,"title":"Any IC changes based upon feedback?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-15T01:11:20-07:00","id":228874,"title":"Any IC changes based upon feedback?","content":"Just curious if any of the writers or developers could comment on if any changes have occurred based upon feedback received from the weekly/bi-weekly posts that Stew had been doing. Examples such as Urshul not applying a persistent defense penalty that lasted for a scene if healed, Hishu gaining +1 to perception, wolf forms gaining higher of wits or dex for defense purposes, Gauru healing changed to not be all bashing and lethal per turn, and different dice modifiers for forms instead of a direct import from W:TF.<br /> <br /> If none have occurred, curious as to why, and if they have occurred, how do the changes feel when compared to before?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T01:14:15-07:00","id":228887,"title":"","content":"Changes have happened, things have been tweaked based on community feedback. However, these have occurred over the last several months and I can't recall specifics at the moment.<br /> <br /> Some of your examples ring bells, but not all.<br /> <br /> (Sorry that's not super helpful.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T01:31:36-07:00","id":228893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=228887#post228887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changes have happened, things have been tweaked based on community feedback. However, these have occurred over the last several months and I can't recall specifics at the moment.<br /> <br /> Some of your examples ring bells, but not all.<br /> <br /> (Sorry that's not super helpful.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Still good to know that community feedback was listened to and acted upon. The examples I listed were actually the original implementations from the initial post by Stew on the different forms. Specifically, they were written originally as follows<br /> <br /> 1) Hishu form had no perception bonus. Proposed change was to give +1 to reflect heightened Uratha senses<br /> 2) Urshul form on a damaging hit, would apply a defense reduction that lasted for the rest of the scene, but didn't stack if the same character damaged twice. Proposed change was to have the defense penalty go away if the character could heal themselves.<br /> 3) Urshul, Urhan, and Gauru form applied defense normally with the exception that it also affected firearms. Proposed change was to use higher of wits or dexterity rather than the lower as most animals used this formula already.<br /> 4) Gauru healing would regenerate all bashing and lethal damage per turn. Proposed changes were numerous with a popular choice being primal urge in bashing/lethal<br /> <br /> BIGGEST ISSUE (for me at least)<br /> 5) Gauru must attack nearest opponent (only bite, claw, or throw) or move towards nearest opponent if can't attack. Doing otherwise risks Kuruth. Proposed change was to allow a bit more freedom and allow types of weaponry such as clubs or axes to allow greater variety \u200band not rule out specific fetish weapons.<br /> <br /> Additional proposed change is to allow the Uratha in Gauru form to focus on a specific target providing they are not in Kuruth. This was to directly address the flaw of being required to attack the closest target which is an extremely exploitable mechanic since a smart enemy can keep rotating injured people out and the Gauru is mechanically incapable of finishing them off as they now must focus on the new target.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T04:45:32-07:00","id":228987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=228893#post228893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Hishu form had no perception bonus. Proposed change was to give +1 to reflect heightened Uratha senses</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure exactly where we are with Hishu changes but I know Bunyip's working on some tracking-related rules, Hishu might have something in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Urshul form on a damaging hit, would apply a defense reduction that lasted for the rest of the scene, but didn't stack if the same character damaged twice. Proposed change was to have the defense penalty go away if the character could heal themselves. </div> </div> </div>Urshul no longer reduces Defence for the rest of the scene on hit; instead its first attack in a scene applies a free Tilt. Broken legs, dislocated arms and gouged eyes ahoy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Urshul, Urhan, and Gauru form applied defense normally with the exception that it also affected firearms. Proposed change was to use higher of wits or dexterity rather than the lower as most animals used this formula already. </div> </div> </div>I think there was discussion about possibly having a Merit with that effect. Not sure, haven't seen the latest revision of the Merits yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Gauru healing would regenerate all bashing and lethal damage per turn. Proposed changes were numerous with a popular choice being primal urge in bashing/lethal </div> </div> </div>Currently Gauru still keeps full regen each turn, we're playtesting it. Seeing a Gauru-specced Rahu get dropped in 2 turns makes me suspect it won't change, but not completel sure yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BIGGEST ISSUE (for me at least)<br /> 5) Gauru must attack nearest opponent (only bite, claw, or throw) or move towards nearest opponent if can't attack. Doing otherwise risks Kuruth. Proposed change was to allow a bit more freedom and allow types of weaponry such as clubs or axes to allow greater variety \u200band not rule out specific fetish weapons. </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen the latest revision of Gauru yet so not sure on this front.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:00:53-07:00","id":229008,"title":"","content":"In the next Forsaken Friday Stew's said he'd answer questions posted in the comments section of the last blog. So you could ask there for clarification on the things Acrozatarim and Bunyip haven't seen yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:10:38-07:00","id":229013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=228987#post228987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Currently Gauru still keeps full regen each turn, we're playtesting it. Seeing a Gauru-specced Rahu get dropped in 2 turns makes me suspect it won't change, but not completel sure yet.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am both glad that you're keeping full regen and that it's not so game-breaking that it can't be gotten around. Like, really happy. I'm glad that my werewolf could solo a tank. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:07:05-07:00","id":229372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=229013#post229013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am both glad that you're keeping full regen and that it's not so game-breaking that it can't be gotten around. Like, really happy. I'm glad that my werewolf could solo a tank. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I also like the tank-soloing ability, but I still have some reservations. Mainly that the full refresh creates a weird incentive to take as much damage as possible before switching to Gauru so you get the most out of the healing, then switch back to another form until you take a lot of damage again. Turns in Gauru becomes number of times you can clear out your health track in one combat, rather than amount of time you can spend in war form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:41:03-07:00","id":229442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=229372#post229372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like the tank-soloing ability, but I still have some reservations. Mainly that the full refresh creates a weird incentive to take as much damage as possible before switching to Gauru so you get the most out of the healing, then switch back to another form until you take a lot of damage again. Turns in Gauru becomes number of times you can clear out your health track in one combat, rather than amount of time you can spend in war form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, you raise a good point. Would a penalty on changing while wounded fix the problem, or a penalty to resisting <i>kuruth</i> if you go Gauru while wounded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T13:58:33-07:00","id":229545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=229372#post229372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like the tank-soloing ability, but I still have some reservations. Mainly that the full refresh creates a weird incentive to take as much damage as possible before switching to Gauru so you get the most out of the healing, then switch back to another form until you take a lot of damage again. Turns in Gauru becomes number of times you can clear out your health track in one combat, rather than amount of time you can spend in war form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you now able to shift into Gauru multiple times per scene now so long as you don't use up all of your turns? Before, you were still only able to assume the form once per scene in W:TF","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:00:29-07:00","id":229548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=229545#post229545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you now able to shift into Gauru multiple times per scene now so long as you don't use up all of your turns? Before, you were still only able to assume the form once per scene in W:TF</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We don't know yet. We know there's an amount of turns you can be in gauru but not much beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:04:12-07:00","id":229551,"title":"","content":"I <i>think </i>it's still once per scene, with certain specific exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:03:28-07:00","id":229656,"title":"","content":"Knowing that, my concerns are at least somewhat alleviated. I'm still iffy on the healing encouraging you to save your one Gauru transformation for when you're full or close to full on Lethal. But yeah, once per scene helps,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:04:09-07:00","id":229659,"title":"","content":"Do the forms keep the same attribute modifiers they had or did they got tweaked after the playstesting with the various new abilities, gifts etc??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":".  error 08-15-2014, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:36:41-07:00","id":229691,"title":"","content":"We haven't seen the second draft of forms yet, so can't answer that with certainty. My playtest group has used the modifiers from WtF so far, which appear to be working well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T23:27:24-07:00","id":230014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=228987#post228987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urshul no longer reduces Defence for the rest of the scene on hit; instead its first attack in a scene applies a free Tilt. Broken legs, dislocated arms and gouged eyes ahoy!</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this feel to you from a gameplay perspective? Being that I can only see what is posted here rather than actual gameplay, this seems very powerful, borderline hax. Right now all I can imagine in 2 Urshul each scoring a hit and suddenly you have an enemy with no defense. While I have no problem with the tilts themselves, it seems a bit unfair that they do not need to take the specific penalty for targeting the appropriate part in order to afflict the tilt. Using blinded as an example, I would normally be required to perform a targeted attack against the eyes to try and apply this condition which carries a significant dice penalty. As an Urshul, I can simply make an attack as normal and still somehow apply it by utilizing a larger dice pool.<br /> <br /> Again, without any gameplay to go on, this is simply my initial thought and it very well could be a knee-jerk reaction. Then again, I am not a fan of what is known is &quot;always the best move&quot; where one specific move is so superior mechanically that it limits gameplay choices simply because not doing it is considered stupid. This was sort of the case with Rite of Dedication and Rite of Healing. Both rituals were seen as so superior to others that not taking them was seen as borderline insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T03:31:51-07:00","id":230091,"title":"","content":"Each form now has a very specific use in the hunt, and Urshul is the &quot;weaken and harass the prey&quot; one. Hence the ability to give a Tilt relatively easy. Note that is only once a Scene, the fact that several Urshul ganging on the same target can bring it down due to acumulated Tilts is the intended result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:19:04-07:00","id":231950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=229656#post229656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing that, my concerns are at least somewhat alleviated. I'm still iffy on the healing encouraging you to save your one Gauru transformation for when you're full or close to full on Lethal. But yeah, once per scene helps,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually like it, for the same reasons as you dislike it. <br /> I think it kinda fits with the setting that have the Werewolves being forced into war form when they are getting hurt a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T17:19:36-07:00","id":232120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=230014#post230014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this feel to you from a gameplay perspective? Being that I can only see what is posted here rather than actual gameplay, this seems very powerful, borderline hax. Right now all I can imagine in 2 Urshul each scoring a hit and suddenly you have an enemy with no defense. While I have no problem with the tilts themselves, it seems a bit unfair that they do not need to take the specific penalty for targeting the appropriate part in order to afflict the tilt. Using blinded as an example, I would normally be required to perform a targeted attack against the eyes to try and apply this condition which carries a significant dice penalty. As an Urshul, I can simply make an attack as normal and still somehow apply it by utilizing a larger dice pool.<br /> <br /> Again, without any gameplay to go on, this is simply my initial thought and it very well could be a knee-jerk reaction. Then again, I am not a fan of what is known is &quot;always the best move&quot; where one specific move is so superior mechanically that it limits gameplay choices simply because not doing it is considered stupid. This was sort of the case with Rite of Dedication and Rite of Healing. Both rituals were seen as so superior to others that not taking them was seen as borderline insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels pretty good in the combats I've run.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by it seeming unfair - unfair against who?<br /> <br /> Rather than enforcing a 'best move', the new Urshul mechanisms have, I've found, done the opposite - my players have had lots of choice over which Tilts they want to use with their limited 'free' capability to deploy them each fight. The only thing I did early on in playtesting was to rule that the Urshul one-free-Tilt power can't apply Stunned, as otherwise you'd just get chained Tilt stun-locks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:14:55-07:00","id":232195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=232120#post232120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It feels pretty good in the combats I've run.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by it seeming unfair - unfair against who?<br /> <br /> Rather than enforcing a 'best move', the new Urshul mechanisms have, I've found, done the opposite - my players have had lots of choice over which Tilts they want to use with their limited 'free' capability to deploy them each fight. The only thing I did early on in playtesting was to rule that the Urshul one-free-Tilt power can't apply Stunned, as otherwise you'd just get chained Tilt stun-locks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply and it puts me greatly at ease to know that there is active play testing going on with the tilts for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> By unfair, I was referring to the fact that many creatures and other supernatural archetypes need to take a massive penalty to a dice pool to try and afflict conditions such as blinded. In many cases this results in a very small dice pool where the success feels good when you pull it off. With the Urshul tilt, I do not need to take the large hit to my dice pool in order to apply the same effect. This becomes more pronounced in the GMC rules update where defense pools are higher and hits land less frequently, but often harder. As for the unfair against who, in my case it would be the Storyteller since it means that any single antagonist they create should be expected to have an exact sequence of events played out against them regardless of the type of fight.<br /> <br /> For example, why have 2 Urshul apply leg Wrack when you can apply 2 instances of Knocked Down or Blinded? Double leg wrack reduces movement rolls to a chance die and knocks down when double knocked down causes them to lose 2 actions (including movement) and take -2 to all attacks in addition to being knocked down? Double blinded kills all defense and makes doing anything visual including combat almost impossible.<br /> <br /> To to try and clarify since it is hard to convey tone and emotion via text on a board, I am not upset or angry at all, I am simply curious since if I can think of it, someone else has been thinking the same thing and not voiced it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T22:11:57-07:00","id":232439,"title":"","content":"When wolves bring down prey they hit the weak spots,snapping at tendons and other important muscle groups, their sole aim being to eliminate the prey's ability to defend itself. The Urshul ability sounds perfectly placed to imitate that instinctual pack method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:27:01-07:00","id":234123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=232195#post232195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the reply and it puts me greatly at ease to know that there is active play testing going on with the tilts for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> By unfair, I was referring to the fact that many creatures and other supernatural archetypes need to take a massive penalty to a dice pool to try and afflict conditions such as blinded. In many cases this results in a very small dice pool where the success feels good when you pull it off. With the Urshul tilt, I do not need to take the large hit to my dice pool in order to apply the same effect. This becomes more pronounced in the GMC rules update where defense pools are higher and hits land less frequently, but often harder. As for the unfair against who, in my case it would be the Storyteller since it means that any single antagonist they create should be expected to have an exact sequence of events played out against them regardless of the type of fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious answer to this is that the Storyteller <i>should expect</i> single, lone antagonists going up against a whole pack of werewolves to be in trouble <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, there are ways and means, as it were. Leg Wracking a spirit with fifteen legs - or no legs at all - will be of limited effect. Blinding a werewolf or other creature that has extremely developed senses is not as effective as it is against, say, a human. Werewolves may regenerate Tilts fairly fast, they have access to a Facet that allows them to regenerate them <i>very</i> fast, and Rahu have a tool for it as well.<br /> <br /> Numbers is also a great advantage against Tilts; piling all your Wracks and Blinds etc on one prey doesn't help much with the other five that are chewing your face off.<br /> <br /> However, yes, Tilts and their application through Urshul and Facets is something I've been examining closely in playtesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, why have 2 Urshul apply leg Wrack when you can apply 2 instances of Knocked Down or Blinded? Double leg wrack reduces movement rolls to a chance die and knocks down when double knocked down causes them to lose 2 actions (including movement) and take -2 to all attacks in addition to being knocked down? Double blinded kills all defense and makes doing anything visual including combat almost impossible. </div> </div> </div>Knocked Down doesn't work quite like you're implying - it only has a chance to cause loss of actions if it occurs before the target has had a chance to act, and even then they get a chance to resist. Blinded is an interesting one because it has two durational effects in its write-up - 1 turn and til damage is healed - and I'm suspecting the free Urshul Tilt version should probably be by default the 1 turn one, unless enough damage is scored - an exceptional success, perhaps - that makes it stick until damage is healed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To to try and clarify since it is hard to convey tone and emotion via text on a board, I am not upset or angry at all, I am simply curious since if I can think of it, someone else has been thinking the same thing and not voiced it. </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I wasn't thinking you were upset or angry. These are all things we're looking at, mulling over and playtesting, and I'm keen to get it right precisely because I don't want to see the same Tilt being applied forever, every time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:26:28-07:00","id":234372,"title":"","content":"You good sir just made my day with this post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T05:33:35-07:00","id":238105,"title":"","content":"Another bit of feedback that I can confirm has changed things a bit - peoples' response to the Sacred Hunt rite. It was generally very positive but plenty of people felt that the ability to hit ephemeral entities didn't seem appropriate to all the different tribes with their various favoured prey.<br /> <br /> I can't say this as a dead cert for what the final version will be like, but it's now looking like the rite will give you different benefits depending on the tribe of the ritemaster, each tailored to the kind of prey the tribe tends to hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:56:08-07:00","id":238292,"title":"","content":"Actually, that sounds like a really good change. While the ephemeral portion never really bothered me, having different flavors depending on the ritemaster's tribe definitely sounds fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:01:16-07:00","id":238642,"title":"","content":"It's a good change IMO. It makes multi-tribe packs more versatile, encourages packs to negotiate with each other to help manage the prey they're less familiar with, and reinforces why it's less optimal forany one tribe to monopolise any territory. (Even though that happens all too frequently.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:20:40-07:00","id":238655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=238642#post238642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good change IMO. It makes multi-tribe packs more versatile, encourages packs to negotiate with each other to help manage the prey they're less familiar with, and reinforces why it's less optimal forany one tribe to monopolise any territory. (Even though that happens all too frequently.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Still should be a pack rite, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:32:21-07:00","id":238665,"title":"","content":"Still a pack rite, yes, however you obviously only get the tribe-specific bonus if the ritemaster's an uratha of that tribe, so a wolf-blooded ritemaster won't give it.<br /> <br /> Unless you have Wolf-Blooded being accepted into tribes, but that would surely be a local or regional oddity and certainly not, say, something that pops up in a Hunting Ground sample location or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T16:57:38-07:00","id":239673,"title":"","content":"Was there any major change to Death Rage since the blog post oh so long ago?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:10:45-07:00","id":240073,"title":"","content":"Depends how you define major change, but there has been a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T21:31:00-07:00","id":241061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=240073#post240073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends how you define major change, but there has been a change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You, my good sir, are a tease.<br /> <br /> And I love you for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T02:45:32-07:00","id":241194,"title":"","content":"What I woulda done with Soft Rage is have it work like how the previewed Chain Rage rite does: You're in it for a number of turns, then you roll Resolve + Composure, and you gotta accumulate a number of successes to be out of it (meanwhile taking Gauru is going into Wasu-Im, and you gotta stick to Urshul or Dalu, and if you shape-shift you gotta make another kinda control roll not to take Gauru reflexively instead.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:06:45-07:00","id":256770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=228987#post228987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently Gauru still keeps full regen each turn, we're playtesting it. Seeing a Gauru-specced Rahu get dropped in 2 turns makes me suspect it won't change, but not completel sure yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>As we are coming in to massive combat in our game were we are speculating our Rahu &quot;monster&quot; ( 14 Health Box in Gauru, Base Strengh 4, Stamina 4, Brawl 4, Giant Merit, Defence 7 ) to be dropped in the middle of 49 Malejin servant demons and let him fight with them. He got lately fetish Full Plate ( Armor 4/2 ) that he can use in Gauru ( making armor to 5/2, it's fetish's only power, really ). From our calculations he would statistically negate all damage to take only 1 Bash per demon.<br /> <br /> So question is this: <b>How many regenerate now Gauru in turn?</b> Because with full Bashings and full Lethal, he IS unkillable without silver. If now consensus is something like all Bashings and Primal Urge per turn Lethals - he can fight, and probably will bearly be missed - take 15 demons attack. Each one of them makes 1B damage. After 15 attacks, our Rahu has 1 Lethal and 13 Bashings. With even Primal Urge 1 he is totally cure - in one turn, after 15 asaults, <b>without spent a single Essence point</b>. That means to stop one Rahu you need something like 30 angry spirits on only him.<br /> <br /> Option with Primal Urge only Bashings and Lethals would make him more to be killed for, but it's somehow unthematical that Gauru won't heal all Bashings, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T20:51:44-07:00","id":256971,"title":"","content":"Remember it's turn limited. How many spirits can he kill in those turns? Not a whole lot I'm betting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T23:45:00-07:00","id":257019,"title":"","content":"New Gauru turn limit is <i>Stamina</i>+<i>Primal Urge</i>+<i>Auspice Renown</i>. He is rather starting werewolf ( we only ended Tribal Initiation on last session, one month from First Change ) and has Stamina 4, Primal Urge 2 and Purity 2. It's 8 turns in Gauru. 8 Turns he will heal <b>all</b> his damage, and kill <b>at least</b> 8 spirits (demons of Rank 2 I assume), probably more. Without <b>any Essence cost</b>. And it's only <b>one Rahu</b>. With other pack members, starting Uratha now could slay <b>armies</b> of lesser spirits.<br /> <br /> And what goes after Gauru turn limit is ended? Character goes in to Death Rage, staying in Gauru as long as it needs, if I remember correctly? So without Essence cost, he <b>IS</b> stoppable, immortal killing machine, because he will in Death Rage regenerate <b>any</b> demage. Basically, with rules show in spoiler, unless someone use silver ( or done Aggravated in other ways ) werewolves are immortal. Even with option of &quot;all Bash and Primal Urge of Lethal&quot; in Gauru.<br /> <br /> If I see spoilers rules correctly, you just drop Uratha in town from the sky, and see as he is living nuclear bomb that slash, kill and destroy any living being in nearest radius. <b>One</b> Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T00:32:35-07:00","id":257023,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing the problem. Werewolves are monstrously capable combatants, and to take just one down requires preparation, skill, equipment, teamwork and luck. You've managed to make a tank Rahu, designed to be the epitome of unkillable combat scariness and you're seemingly complaining that it is almost unkillable and scary in combat...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T00:33:24-07:00","id":257025,"title":"","content":"Healing all bashing and Primal Urge lethal actually wouldn't make much of a difference in your example. The Gauru would still heal the 13 bashing and 1 lethal per round. I don't think any of the game lines are balanced around the assumption the players are in plate or riot gear. If the Storyteller gives the player magic full plate and situations where they can use it, then they shouldn't be surprised that it is hard to hurt them during some of those situations.<br /> <br /> Armor and full regeneration are strong, but there are plenty of ways to still make the fight interesting. Presumably the demons have Numina or Influences that can tilt the odds in there favor. If not, why even bother playing things out? Dozens of identical spirits that have no special abilities seems like the kind of fodder that Down&amp;Dirty combat is made for, especially given that the designers specifically mention Down&amp;Dirty fighting against equal or lower ranked spirits in the Gauru rules preview. Let's assume though that we really want to play out a fight involving perfectly generic low-ranked Maeljin foot soldiers and we want the demons to win, force a retreat, or at least expend some of the Gauru's resources before the main fight. The Gauru is probably only rolling around 11 to 13 dice without spending Essence or Willpower. Even a Rank 1 Spirits can reach defense 8 if they buff their attributes. The Gauru probably eats one in round one. After that, the Maeljin can just dodge until war form runs out, spending willpower on the contested dodge roll. Why bog down the game doing 15-49 attack rolls a turn that you don't think matter when you can just declare they're dodging, let the player whiff for 8 attacks and then they're back to Dalu or Ushul for the rest of the fight? If the Rahu is soloing the combat like the example suggests it would only take a few minutes of table time to run out the clock. Once they're back down to normal werewolf regeneration, I think the player would feel differently about all of the nickel and dime damage coming their way.<br /> <br /> Death Rage duration is based on Primal Urge. It starts at around 10 minutes and reaches 12 hours at Primal Urge 10. After that, the Uratha &quot;collapses&quot; in Hishu form. If a low Primal Urge werewolf is dropped into enemy territory and then Death Rages, there's a good chance that at least one enemy managed to run or hide long enough to kill the kamikaze berserker once the rage ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 09-15-2014, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T01:02:01-07:00","id":257038,"title":"","content":"<b>My general point:</b> I think that werewolves should be combat monsters. They SHOULD be able to withstand massive damage. But <b>not</b> to be immortal in reality. Werewolves should be killable by groups of ( non-soldier) hunters with non-silver weapons, taking maybe even 10 of them for it, in once fight. But not destroying whole towns, on itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257023#post257023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing the problem. Werewolves are monstrously capable combatants, and to take just one down requires preparation, skill, equipment, teamwork and luck. You've managed to make a tank Rahu, designed to be the epitome of unkillable combat scariness and you're seemingly complaining that it is almost unkillable and scary in combat...?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, that he is UNKILLABLE. With full Bashing and Lethal regen in Gauru, character is in reality, immortal - lowest character in nWoD starts with Stamina 1, Size 4 ( Small Frame ). Give him Primal Urge 1 and Primary Renown 1 and character can have 3 turns of 14 Health ( Stamina 1 + Size 6 in Gauru, 7 Health boxes ) for free. More, when you seen last that character done more damage than 8L in combat? Because to let put down this &quot;beast&quot; ( and it's weakest possible werewolf you can make ) you need to make 8L each turn ( to mark at least one Aggravated demage that will last after next turn ), for about 7 of them, and prayer that this beast don't kill you all in those 3 turns when she is using her own special powers. WEAKEST. POSSIBLE. CHARACTER.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257025#post257025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Rage duration is based on Primal Urge. It starts at around 10 minutes and reaches 12 hours at Primal Urge 10. After that, the Uratha &quot;collapses&quot; in Hishu form. If a low Primal Urge werewolf is dropped into enemy territory and then Death Rages, there's a good chance that at least one enemy managed to run or hide long enough to kill the kamikaze berserker once the rage ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>This rules I overlooked and if there is really a ticking time limit for Death Rage, it is possible to kill immortal Uratha, just you need to wait for it. But if he goes to Hishu even for one turn, couldn't he just take next Gauru form and time limits are reseted? That would mean characters have only one turn to kill monster - once more, immortality of werewolves in practice.<br /> <br /> I'm still in favor of regeneration in Gauru as &quot;full Bashing and Primal Urge in Lethals per turn&quot;. It's still VERY tough, and old wolves are real monsters. But younger Uratha are killable in fight, by very desperate mortals - very much like in monster movies game tries to emulate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-15-2014, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T01:25:03-07:00","id":257054,"title":"","content":"I'm rather suspicious of this whole scenario.<br /> <br /> I mean... 49 spirits... stated how? I mean, even at Rank 2, if they have Power 6/Finesse 6/Resistance 2 and Blast... they should have zero trouble blowing this Rahu to hell in a single round. With their 12 dice attack pools, the Rahu's Defense probably isn't high enough (-2 from the armor and goes down each attack)... and if they all target around the armor (-3 to -5 depending on how your rule it), out of 49 nine of them enough are going to get lucky that he'll be well into full lethal and rolling over into Agg, if he even survives.<br /> <br /> Edit... actually... how does he even survive 49 bashing damage in one round wrapping around? Unless WtF 2e changes how healing works (making it per attack instead of once a turn, which it does not sound like it is the case), 49 Bashing against a 14 health target = death from Agg roll over (even if barely). They all just pummel him with ranged attacks and the roll over kills him before he regens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-15-2014, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T01:37:01-07:00","id":257060,"title":"","content":"It's like one of those scenes in the movies where the werewolf wakes up naked and covered in blood the next day with no idea what happened. &quot;Once the Basu-Im is over, she collapses into Hishu with no memory of what she has done.&quot; I'm pretty sure the intent is that the Uratha is unconscious and unable to Death Rage again until they wake up/next scene. Even if the werewolf woke up after just one attack, that attack would benefit from the Killing Blows rule. A rank 1 spirit could do 13 automatic damage if their attributes were focused on Power and Finesse and they buffed before the swing. A Rank 2 spirit could do 21 damage--more with a weapon. Either one would be enough to cause the stunned tilt.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, the armor is the main culprit for the Rahu's survivability in your example. Without it, the spirits would do pretty well in swarming the Rahu, especially if he doesn't have a way to prevent the defense penalty caused by defending against multiple attacks in a round. Remember, Gauru probably doesn't have natural armor anymore. At least, Bunyip thought they didn't when the question came up in the shape changing preview thread. Admittedly, we never got an 100% official answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 09-15-2014, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T01:49:17-07:00","id":257062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257054#post257054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... 49 spirits... stated how? I mean, even at Rank 2, if they have Power 6/Finesse 6/Resistance 2 and Blast... they should have zero trouble blowing this Rahu to hell in a single round.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Rank 2 as beings strong, but moderate power. So if Rank 1 spirit is something like normal human ( Power 2/Finesse 2/Resistance 2 ), Rank 2 is more like very strong human ( Power 4/Finesse 3/Resistance 2, and a like ). I can't truly envision spirit/demon of Rank 2 with something more like 5 in Attribute outside of very specific occasions. Rank 3 is for truly inhuman beings with Attributes 6+.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257054#post257054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With their 12 dice attack pools, the Rahu's Defense probably isn't high enough (-2 from the armor and goes down each attack)...and if they all target around the armor (-3 to -5 depending on how your rule it), out of 49 nine of them enough are going to get lucky that he'll be well into full lethal and rolling over into Agg, if he even survives.</div> </div> </div> </div>On <b>GMC</b> rules ( or <b>TSS 2nd Ed</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) that we use Armor aren't added to Defense - it's limit damage taken by character. So in our fight if demons rolls 5 Damage dices after taking characters Defence 7 in Gauru - it's 5 dices. So it's about 2 Lethal damage statistically from each attack. With Gauru natural armor negating 1 Lethal, it's 1 Lethal damage on players character from attack. Half Plate in here don't change - characters in Armor always take at least 1 Bashing damage from each attack, even if damage would be 0 or lower. So it's more problem only 1 Lethal or 1 Bashing per attack. It's more 14 or 28 demons to go to Aggravated level. But it's not problem, I could just throw more of them.<br /> <br /> Problem is &quot;werewolves in Gauru can't be killed by normal humans&quot; or even &quot;can't be killed by group of normal hunters&quot;. <b>Starting Rahu character</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-15-2014, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:05:36-07:00","id":257068,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm still not seeing the problem. The moral of the story is &quot;don't fight uratha in gauru form&quot;?<br /> Acrozaritam (sp?) has even said his/her playtest group lost a character *despite* the healing abilities of gauru. If I recall correctly it was at the claws of another werewolf, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> So you say it can't happen, evidence says it can. I say it's bloody difficult but can be done. I reckon ten mortal humans with military gear could take one down with preparation. Traps, tricks and a helluva lot of lead rain. Throw in a grenade or two and who needs silver?<br /> <br /> Oh that's right, people who want to kill werewolves need silver. Exactly as the legends say!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:24:31-07:00","id":257079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257068#post257068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you say it can't happen, evidence says it can. I say it's bloody difficult but can be done. I reckon ten mortal humans with military gear could take one down with preparation. Traps, tricks and a helluva lot of lead rain. Throw in a grenade or two and who needs silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Traps are good - but they effect will disappear after one turn in Gauru, with rules the same as in spoilers. I don't know any traps that makes Aggravated damage. Bear Trap makes 3L - so you need to roll character with 5 of then to make Uratha <b>any</b> lasting damage.<br /> <br /> A bit absurd i must say...<br /> <br /> What damage do the grenade? I can't find them in <b>GMC</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257068#post257068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh that's right, people who want to kill werewolves need silver. Exactly as the legends say!</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that you as mortal can kill them ONLY with silver. To make them lasting damage you need at least 15+ Lethal damage per turn - what non-soldier specific character, or even 3 of them, can done this for beasts with Defense of 6-7? Any one? If you don't have Weaponry 4/Firearms 4 and Strengh 4/Dexterity 4? In other words - if your character isn't made specify killer, how can you kill now Gauru?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:27:26-07:00","id":257096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257038#post257038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My general point:</b> I think that werewolves should be combat monsters. They SHOULD be able to withstand massive damage. But <b>not</b> to be immortal in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've said it before Wyrdhamster, but it's worth saying again - you're operating on incomplete information. Your play test game doesn't have all the info. You make incorrect assumptions because you haven't got the full info yet, and that makes your experience less than optimal.<br /> <br /> Werewolves in 2nd ed aren't immortal. Gauru in 2nd ed aren't immortal. <br /> <br /> Until the final text is released you're going to keep encountering these difficulties and being forced to make choices in how to deal with them - many of which may cause frustration.<br /> <br /> Sorry that this is frustrating. We writers can't give away all the answers. We've probably given just about as many spoilers as we can without Stew sending out the NDA police.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:28:01-07:00","id":257113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257062#post257062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Problem is &quot;<b>werewolves in Gauru can't be killed by normal humans</b>&quot; or even &quot;<i>can't be killed by group of normal hunters</i>&quot;. <b>Starting Rahu character</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> what non-soldier specific character, or even 3 of them, can done this for beasts with Deffence of 6-7? Any one? If you don't have Weaponry 4/Firearms 4 and Strengh 4/Dexterity4? In other words - if your character isn't made specify killer, how can you kill now Gauru?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the bold: So average joes cannot kill half-spirit apex predators when they assume their giant primeval furball of death form? Works as intended, I believe.<br /> <br /> For the italic: Hunters so uninformed or cocky that hunt the above creatures without packing silver, deserve the horrible deaths they will receive.<br /> <br /> For the last part: Again why should characters with no combat training be able to kill werewolves in Gauru with no silver?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Also as Bunyip said, you make too many assumptions that we do not know if they are correct (well he does <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 09-15-2014, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:46:32-07:00","id":257122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257062#post257062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Rank 2 as beings strong, but moderate power. So if Rank 1 spirit is something like normal human ( Power 2/Finesse 2/Resistance 2 ), Rank 2 is more like very strong human ( Power 4/Finesse 3/Resistance 2, and a like ). I can't truly envision spirit/demon of Rank 2 with something more like 5 in Attribute outside of very specific occasions. Rank 3 is for truly inhuman beings with Attributes 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's doesn't follow the rules in the books.<br /> <br /> Rank 2 Ephemeral entities have a Trait limit of 7 (which can be boosted to 9 I might add), and between 9-14 dots in them. A 4/3/2 spirit is the low end of Rank 2 power. Even if you go evenly spread out 5/5/4 is also in the Rank 2 range. And they could spend two turns and 4 Essence (still having 11 left) to be 9/9/4 for the scene, giving them a Defense of 9 and 18 dice attack pools, and an 11 base initiative. Your example character's Defense was only 7 (you didn't state if that was before or after armor). That can easily leave them plenty of dice to target around armor and still beat out the 1 innate Gauru form Armor.<br /> <br /> And having the Blast Numina makes this worse since it gives them a +2L ranged attack option. So that would give them 8 dice to target the head (not inherently covered by plate). You don't need 49 of such characters to kill this Rahu before he can even do anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On <b>GMC</b> rules ( or <b>TSS 2nd Ed</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) that we use Armor aren't added to Defense - it's limit damage taken by character. </div> </div> </div>I was taking this into account.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem is &quot;werewolves in Gauru can't be killed by normal humans&quot; or even &quot;can't be killed by group of normal hunters&quot;. <b>Starting Rahu character</b>. </div> </div> </div>A bunch of poorly stated for combat characters sucking against a Rahu in Gauru doesn't make for proof of the point.<br /> <br /> I can easily stat up a squad of humans that, if you ignore Lunacy, would easily beat this werewolf in a few rounds with minimal risk to themselves through firepower and good tactics.<br /> <br /> This whole &quot;invincibility&quot; thing is built on why most people don't like white-room situations. You're just stating a hypothetical in the werewolf's favor, not actually trying to think about what it would take for a squad of hunters to get around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:57:43-07:00","id":257127,"title":"","content":"OK..<br /> <br /> 49 Maeljin servant demons..That is a lot of actions for one ST to plan! O.o<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I am just playing W:tF games with a different scale of combat than others here.<br /> Werewolf is chaotic, it is grim and it has teeth. It is a game were every hunt matters and it could be a fatal one if the prey is dangerous and has the right advantages. If you always hunt to kill then the prey will soon enough find new ways to stop you.<br /> If not, well then I don't think the ST is pulling his/her weight.<br /> The way I see it, prey does not always need to die, only that it is hunted. The resolution should always be more than just to cue the fight.<br /> <br /> In a horror-game I think each encounter should be a real experience for the players. One spirit should be make any PC Uratha feel the need to rethink their &quot;kill-all&quot; strategy.<br /> <br /> When the game turns into furries that wades through challenges like butter.. Well lets just say I agree to disagree :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T05:25:50-07:00","id":257215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257079#post257079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Traps are good - but they effect will disappear after one turn in Gauru, with rules the same as in spoilers. I don't know any traps that makes Aggravated damage. Bear Trap makes 3L - so you need to roll character with 5 of then to make Uratha <b>any</b> lasting damage.<br /> <br /> A bit absurd i must say...<br /> <br /> What damage do the grenade? I can't find them in <b>GMC</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Problem is that you as mortal can kill them ONLY with silver. To make them lasting damage you need at least 15+ Lethal damage per turn - what non-soldier specific character, or even 3 of them, can done this for beasts with Defense of 6-7? Any one? If you don't have Weaponry 4/Firearms 4 and Strengh 4/Dexterity 4? In other words - if your character isn't made specify killer, how can you kill now Gauru?</div> </div> </div> </div>The trap isn't there to kill the werewolf, it's to slow them down, so doing aggravated damage is unnecessary. Not sure why you would think throwing five bear traps at a uratha was what I meant. Sounds absurd.<br /> <br /> Look in Armory, Armory Reloaded, and Dogs of War (especially) for heavier weapons and explosives.<br /> <br /> Have you ever seen a movie or read a story where the raging werewolf was *not* killed by silver in the half-man-half-wolf form? Why is that so unreasonable? If you don't want to need silver, wait until the werewolf is in human form, just like in the stories, when it will be much easier. If you think waiting is too hard, yeah... it probably is, so maybe you should avoid being prey, and hunt the uratha on your own terms? Find where it lives, ambush it while asleep, rig the car it drives to work every morning - cut the brakes, add some dynamite, whatever.<br /> <br /> Of course that's hard too. Especially if the werewolf has a pack.<br /> <br /> So yeah... you might want to get silver. And hide. And get your own allies. Lots of them.<br /> <br /> Fact is, they can die. They can even die in gauru to other werewolves, powerful spirits, elder vampires, and so on. Yes, even supercharged tank Rahu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T10:53:11-07:00","id":257395,"title":"","content":"I watched the 2011 <i>Wolfman</i> recently. In it, the wolfman kills probably around a dozen hunters in the English woods around his home. This being the same movie where a single shot from a revolver with silver bullets kills a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Now, I get that this isn't <i>Wolfman: The RPG</i>, and I'm grateful for that, but I can't imagine why you'd expect or <i>want</i> any different outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T13:56:31-07:00","id":257587,"title":"","content":"I think, as seems the case with most, that we're ignoring the purpose of gauru. It's a war form, unstoppable, and damn near terrifying by sight alone.<br /> <br /> Personally for my Cahalith, unless i'm going out of my way to terrify someone, I'm saving gauru for a big situation. I keep it like my heavy ammunition in destiny. So what if people do the same? <br /> <br /> As for time limit problems, if one turn = 3 seconds, and he gets 11 turns, he's still out of the form in less then a minute in actual time. Think of it like a mobile howitzer. Your 49 spirits are going to burn him down in a matter of seconds so as that flash runs out. Hell if anything I'd use the form to GET AWAY from the mob of spirits. It isn't a surrender so much as a tactical retreat. No ban violation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T14:29:34-07:00","id":257601,"title":"","content":"Unless they qualify for down and dirt, 49 spirits equals 49 attacks a turn.<br /> <br /> A werewolf only has one.<br /> <br /> The odds speak for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T15:50:02-07:00","id":257666,"title":"","content":"&quot;Every time your character applies his Defense against an attack, reduce his Defense by one until the start of the next turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1 vs 49, yeah, that werewolf is going down unless he pulls out an area attack or something (gift of the elements and four purity renown can create fire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-15-2014, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T17:13:55-07:00","id":257699,"title":"","content":"With a group that large if your ST is letting them all get in hits on one target on the same round my suspension of disbelief gets broken. All those spirits in the way will be blocking lines of sight and fire. That's something that I would like to see addressed with a couple of sentences either in the Forsaken core book (or the upcoming WoD Hurt Locker book.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T17:43:46-07:00","id":257714,"title":"","content":"I still hold the 1 vs 49 seems a bit much even for a maximum PU werewolf. Even if all 49 are rank 1, all it takes is stall tactics and you would have Werewolf ala mode","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T19:30:52-07:00","id":257777,"title":"","content":"So the takeaway seems to be that the findings are bullshit, Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Juuuust saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T19:51:53-07:00","id":257797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257699#post257699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a group that large if your ST is letting them all get in hits on one target on the same round my suspension of disbelief gets broken. All those spirits in the way will be blocking lines of sight and fire. That's something that I would like to see addressed with a couple of sentences either in the Forsaken core book (or the upcoming WoD Hurt Locker book.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In general yeah.<br /> <br /> Though keep in mind that a spirit with Power 7 and the Blast Numina has a range of 70 yards. Getting 49 people arranged without interfering with each other with that kind of range really isn't that hard.<br /> <br /> Consider one person standing in the middle of a football field. If you say that each spirit takes up 2 yards of space, you could easily line up half of them on one goal line (over 53 yards long), half on the other goal line, and they would all have zero overlap or crossfire issue.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about guns where you don't want them lined up across from each other because the bullets will travel much farther, you can easily space people out using the stands and not have issues with it.<br /> <br /> Of course, that requires a stadium in an otherwise white-room.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine any sort of realistic situation that might come up that this would not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T19:56:01-07:00","id":257803,"title":"","content":"I think in the example given there was just one werewolf, separate from the pack, with 49 spirits.<br /> <br /> But, in regards to Heavy Arms' post. Should spirits be able to hurt other spirits of the same resonance with resonance-based attacks? A rank 1 fire spirit blasting another rank 1 fire spirit, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T21:11:49-07:00","id":257834,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that would be more of a Influence contest than smacking each other with Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T01:41:29-07:00","id":257979,"title":"","content":"So long post, as I try to answer all of you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And I have other question: If werewolf really kill spirit/demon in Shadow Realm, isn\u2019t this being able to reform after a week time? So even if character will kill all 49 spirits, isn\u2019t they returning week later?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257714#post257714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still hold the 1 vs 49 seems a bit much even for a maximum PU werewolf. Even if all 49 are rank 1, all it takes is stall tactics and you would have Werewolf ala mode</div> </div> </div> </div>It was envisioned by me as PACK problem - or even \u201cover our heads, we must think something different\u201d problem. I was thinking that 49 demons should makes starting werewolves pack in terror. But players made those simulation, and I tended to agree with him, before you pointed me to couple of rules in this topic. Thanks every one for asserting my inner ST rule judgment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257803#post257803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the example given there was just one werewolf, separate from the pack, with 49 spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is idea of tanking Rahu player - to drop him in middle of demons and let his Guru and Death Rage solve all the problems. And it makes me very mixed feeling about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257587#post257587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for time limit problems, if one turn = 3 seconds, and he gets 11 turns, he's still out of the form in less then a minute in actual time. Think of it like a mobile howitzer. Your 49 spirits are going to burn him down in a matter of seconds so as that flash runs out. Hell if anything I'd use the form to GET AWAY from the mob of spirits. It isn't a surrender so much as a tactical retreat. No ban violation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is with Gauru regeneration and Death Rage rules, at least what we know about them. Character can destroy one spirit per turn ( more or less ). Spirits, realistic, can make him only about 15 Bashings damage per turn ( each spirit can only make 1 Bash per Armor rules, see below, about spirits line of sight and attack ), and in this it\u2019s about 1 Lethal per turn - that this character can easily regenerate each turn. Maybe it\u2019s 49 Bashing damage, but it would be very suspension of disbelief, and is killing character in first turn ( he can withstand 3*14 Bashings, so it\u2019s 42 damage before killing it).<br /> <br /> Other thing is that if character withstand this attacks and really kill each demon in time of one per turn, he will only need 50 turns to solve problems, and get out of the combat unscratched. And 50 turns is only 2 minutes and 10 seconds - starting, Primal Urge 1 character enter in to Death Rage \u201cfor something like 10 minutes\u201d ( as was stated in spoiler, I suspect 5 minutes for PU 1 and 10 minutes for PU 2 ). So, in theory, PU 2<br /> character taking 1 Bashing by each 49 attacks can withstand, and gone from combat unscratched. At least until you take \u201clower Defense rule\u201d (see below).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257601#post257601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they qualify for down and dirt, 49 spirits equals 49 attacks a turn.<br /> <br /> A werewolf only has one.<br /> <br /> The odds speak for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think that Down and Dirty rules applies, as the sheer combat force is too big for character. And still I needed to make 49 combat rolls for PC vs demons. I think it\u2019s need more Calculus and Logic rules, like \u201cstatistical attack and defense\u201d. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to how many attacks, see next answer below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257699#post257699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a group that large if your ST is letting them all get in hits on one target on the same round my suspension of disbelief gets broken. All those spirits in the way will be blocking lines of sight and fire. That's something that I would like to see addressed with a couple of sentences either in the Forsaken core book (or the upcoming WoD Hurt Locker book.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it possible to make 49 attacks? Can really each epidermal being in Shadow Realm attack him? Can they \u201cstand\u201d in the same place in Shadow Realm, in the same turn? As like can monsters in D&amp;D stand on the same square in times of combat for flanking?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img4.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20120719203117/dnd4/images/d/d8/Flanking.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Truly, I\u2019m asking, as I really don\u2019t know how it is solved in <b>GMC</b>. From \u201cD&amp;D take\u201d it would be only 9 spirits per turn that can reach character. If spirits can take their \u201csquares\u201d, like Demon 13, 17 and 37 attack from the same - it\u2019s makes in reality 49 attacks per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=257666#post257666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Every time your character applies his Defense against an attack, reduce his Defense by one until the start of the next turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1 vs 49, yeah, that werewolf is going down unless he pulls out an area attack or something (gift of the elements and four purity renown can create fire).</div> </div> </div> </div>Overlooked this rule - really, this solves much of one vs many combats problems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T01:47:15-07:00","id":257981,"title":"","content":"Death rage is reactive to situations though. Would an uratha in Gauru truly try to fight and kill ALL 49 enemies? Or is he more likely to claw his way through them and make an escape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T02:53:28-07:00","id":257994,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, an ephemeral entity is only truly destroyed if they lose all of their Essence in addition to their Corpus. There's a rite that lets werewolves devour the essence of a defeated spirit that is the target of a sacred hunt. It's considered disrespectful to drain a spirits Essence completely with the rite, but it is possible. It's impractical for killing multiple spirits at once though. It's also usually a harmony breaking point towards spirit. If a werewolf is using it to systematically kill off a lot of spirits they would probably end up trapped in the Shadow. There's a merit that also damages Essence, but it only depletes 1 or 2 Essence per hit as part of an attack. It's enough to force a Spirit to be careful, but it's unlikely to kill a spirit unless they are reckless. Ephemeral entities do lose Essence when they take Aggravated damage though, so manifesting in the presence of someone holding their bane is very risky for them. For similar reasons, Spirits (But not ghosts or angels, etc) have to be very wary of angering Werewolves that have a high enough honorary rank to inflict aggravated damage against them.<br /> <br /> We don't know whether Death Rage still has a flight response. I suspect it does, but we don't really know. For that matter, we don't know if a werewolf that has already used up their war form for the scene can still shift to Gauru during Wasu-im and voluntarily enter a Death Rage. We only know that they will shift to Gauru during Basu-im. I'm not convinced that a PU 2/Purity 2 Rahu is going to be able to kill a spirit every round, but this discussion is getting a little off track from the thread topic as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T03:34:28-07:00","id":258003,"title":"","content":"Gauru no longer has any armour by default, I think.<br /> <br /> nWoD doesn't use the flanking/positioning/etc rules of a game like D&amp;D. Run it narratively. I'd have it be a fairly epic brawl with the tidal wave of Wounded spirits pouring in, hammering at the gauru as it flails and rends through them. Using All-Out Attacks, Willpower and Essence to boost dice pools and stats means the spirits will probably carve the gauru up in short order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T05:52:31-07:00","id":258065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=258003#post258003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD doesn't use the flanking/positioning/etc rules of a game like D&amp;D. Run it narratively.</div> </div> </div> </div>But power and Gauru form works in <b>turns</b>, not narration. Main problem for now to decide if 15 demons in turn can attack or all of them at once is this - are spirits corporal for one another in Shadow Realm? Because if they Corpus works like human flesh in Material, that means the spirits/demons can't occupy the same space in one turn, as they &quot;bodies&quot; can overlap - the same way two humans can be in same spot ( at least without magic ).<br /> <br /> Are spirits &quot;ephemeral&quot; or &quot;corporal&quot; to one another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T07:12:03-07:00","id":258093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=258065#post258065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But power and Gauru form works in <b>turns</b>, not narration. Main problem for now to decide if 15 demons in turn can attack or all of them at once is this - are spirits corporal for one another in Shadow Realm? Because if they Corpus works like human flesh in Material, that means the spirits/demons can't occupy the same space in one turn, as they &quot;bodies&quot; can overlap - the same way two humans can be in same spot ( at least without magic ).<br /> <br /> Are spirits &quot;ephemeral&quot; or &quot;corporal&quot; to one another?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The word you're looking for is corporeal. Though I think corporal fits too.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't matter. DnD logic works off the assumption that things are, generally, humanoid in shape and on the ground. Standing in a room of 49 spirits can be the equivalent of standing in a fishtank full of 49 piranha. DnD maps are 2d. The narrative approach is not. The rest depends on the ST. They don't need to stand, unless the ST deems it so. Each spirit could be a tentacle, easily whipping around its cousins to lash at the werewolf, if the ST deems it so.. If you have all the spirits be man-shaped and nothing but, then yes, they'd get in each others way, but you've said nothing like that in your scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-16-2014, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:54:16-07:00","id":258190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=258065#post258065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But power and Gauru form works in <b>turns</b>, not narration. Main problem for now to decide if 15 demons in turn can attack or all of them at once is this - are spirits corporal for one another in Shadow Realm? Because if they Corpus works like human flesh in Material, that means the spirits/demons can't occupy the same space in one turn, as they &quot;bodies&quot; can overlap - the same way two humans can be in same spot ( at least without magic ).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still part of the problem with any sort of white-room analysis. 49 creatures trying to pour down a narrow hallway is vastly different from 49 creatures surrounding you in an open field; grid based or narration based positioning.<br /> <br /> This is why I brought up how the spirits in question are built, because that also matters. Most spirits are only Rank in Size. So a 49 Rank 2 spirits are also 49 Size 2 things, which means a lot more of them can attack a Size 8 Gauru form Rahu at once. We're talking about getting swarmed by things the size of cats and medium birds, not human sized entities. Consider that we're not talking about how many human-sized things can gang up effectively on one human-sized thing. We're talking about how many cat-sized things can gang up on a bear-sized thing. Suddenly the idea that 15 of them can attack at once doesn't really sound so hard does it?<br /> <br /> This is also, as nofather pointed out, a 3D environment. Two spirits can't just occupy the same space, but they also aren't bound by a grid system that says 1 creature per X. <br /> <br /> What Influences do these spirits have? What Numina? How are they stated? How smart are they fighting? Do they have weapons (like are they a bunch of imps with pitchforks)?<br /> <br /> Getting hung up on the spacing kind of misses the larger point. It is, in many ways, the least important consideration to how big of a threat a swarm of spirits is going to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T09:53:24-07:00","id":258247,"title":"","content":"In the Shadow, spirits are corporeal to each other and, indeed, everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T11:57:15-07:00","id":258342,"title":"","content":"Should read the intro to lodges the faithful. That pack enters the hisil, is swarmed by spirits and instantly bails out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:48:53-07:00","id":282832,"title":"","content":"I've been wondering how much of the spoilered items in Stew's blog would still remain true for the purposes of playtesting. Not asking for more spoilers, not even for the actual changes (if indeed there are); I just wish to know which of the stuff I'd be able to use now, without needing to &quot;start from a clean save&quot;, so to speak, once the 2e book comes out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T20:19:16-07:00","id":283152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=258342#post258342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should read the intro to lodges the faithful. That pack enters the hisil, is swarmed by spirits and instantly bails out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those things did Aggravated off the bat from what I can read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T20:20:19-07:00","id":283154,"title":"","content":"How can you stop Wasu-Im now, tho? Because by reading the post that's a later inclusion from the playerbase's input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:09:56-07:00","id":283252,"title":"","content":"I'm going to remain highly skeptical of the regeneration rules right up until I have the book in proverbial hand and get a chance to test it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T00:19:25-07:00","id":283607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=282832#post282832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering how much of the spoilered items in Stew's blog would still remain true for the purposes of playtesting. Not asking for more spoilers, not even for the actual changes (if indeed there are); I just wish to know which of the stuff I'd be able to use now, without needing to &amp;quot;start from a clean save&amp;quot;, so to speak, once the 2e book comes out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Changes and additions happened, but you should be right with most of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T00:51:11-07:00","id":283620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228874-any-ic-changes-based-upon-feedback?p=283607#post283607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changes and additions happened, but you should be right with most of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Bunyip!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}